    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d673">

                <pb facs="0795" n="683" sameAs="frus:frus1935v03/pg683"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/13049: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Hankow</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Josselyn</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Hankow</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-04-26T17:00:00+08:00">April 26, 1935—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 26—9:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>14. Reference Nanking telegram April 25, 2 p.m.,<anchor n="97" xml:id="d673-f1"/>
                    reporting information regarding Szechuan received from French Legation
                    representative. Reports received from Chengtu indicate situation that area much
                    improved due to the arrival reenforcements. Some Americans have evacuated and
                    they have sufficient motor transportation to evacuate remainder if necessary but
                    they consider no danger surprise attack and probably will remain for the
                    present. Repeated to the Legation and Nanking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Josselyn</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
